we're seeking feedback on three  infrastructure projects in this year's  draft annual plan  a new community hub is an exciting  addition to the regeneration area in  kaiapoi and a concept plan for the hub  was approved in the ltp along with  funding towards build costs  as the plan developed infrastructure  needed to prepare the site for the new  buildings changed significantly and the  budget needs to be increased  we're also seeking your feedback on  funding increases for stormwater work in  kaiapoi  through the government's shovel ready  fund the council received funding  towards stormwater and flood  improvements this work is essential to  prevent future flooding in kaiapoi  project costs were underestimated and  the cost of construction materials has  risen  this means that the council's  contribution of 50 of the total project  cost needs to increase so that we can  complete it within the government's time  frame  the final topic we want to talk to you  about is funding for road improvements  to fund our work program to upgrade  roads across the district we rely on  funding assistance from wakako tahi  in this funding round we were allocated  half of the cost this means we need to  re-prioritise our work program and focus  on smaller projects that keep our  communities safe  let us know what you think at  govt dot nz forward slash let's talk
 

